WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.559
Disinfectants, Sanitiser, Labelling and Growing the Business. This is module 5, the last module of the course.

2
00:00:08.973 --> 00:00:13.722
These products protect health, so they carry the strictest rules. Let's get them right.

3
00:00:14.722 --> 00:00:22.139
Watch this counter being sprayed and wiped with detergent first. Dirt and grease shield germs and use up disinfectant.

4
00:00:22.586 --> 00:00:26.302
So the order is always: clean first, rinse, then disinfect.

5
00:00:27.302 --> 00:00:33.183
Before you dilute bleach, put on gloves and eye protection. Use cool water in a ventilated space.

6
00:00:34.183 --> 00:00:42.431
These cups go from strong bleach down to weak dilution. You work it out with C1 times V1 equals C2 times V2.

7
00:00:42.837 --> 00:00:56.895
Grace in Ilorin needed 0.1% for floors and 0.5% for a spill kit. Both took about 286 ml of her 3.5% bleach, just made up to different volumes.

8
00:00:57.346 --> 00:01:02.278
She labels each bucket with strength, date and time, and never tops up an old bucket.

9
00:01:03.278 --> 00:01:08.351
Keep these two apart. Never mix bleach with acids, ammonia or other cleaners.

10
00:01:08.679 --> 00:01:17.065
Store diluted bleach in labelled containers, out of sunlight and away from children. Rinse metal surfaces after the contact time.

11
00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:24.891
See the surface stay wet while the timer runs. That's contact time, and wiping dry too early is a common failure.

12
00:01:25.278 --> 00:01:36.571
Quats like BKC are inactivated by soap residue, so rinse first. Musa weighed 40 g of 50% concentrate into about 9 litres, then topped up to 10.

13
00:01:37.571 --> 00:01:47.838
Words like disinfectant or kills 99.9% of germs are health claims. In Nigeria they need NAFDAC registration and efficacy tests.

14
00:01:48.328 --> 00:01:54.512
Until then, sell honestly as cleaners, and teach customers to use registered disinfectants correctly.

15
00:01:55.512 --> 00:02:02.141
Now the hand rub. These cylinders hold alcohol, hydrogen peroxide and glycerol, the WHO formula.

16
00:02:02.498 --> 00:02:10.111
The peroxide deals with spores, and the glycerol protects skin. Change the formula and it's no longer the WHO formulation.

17
00:02:11.111 --> 00:02:19.480
Methanol is poisonous through the skin and if swallowed. Buy ethanol or isopropyl alcohol with a certificate of analysis.

18
00:02:19.937 --> 00:02:29.219
Alcohol vapour catches fire easily. Mix by an open window with no flames, no cooking gas, no smoking and no generator nearby.

19
00:02:30.219 --> 00:02:36.931
Hadiza in Sokoto checked her ethanol with an alcoholmeter. It was 90%, not 96%.

20
00:02:37.275 --> 00:02:47.471
So she measured 1,778 ml instead of 1,667 ml, and the finished rub still reached 80%.

21
00:02:48.471 --> 00:02:56.623
Fill, close and label every bottle with the alcohol percentage, batch number, date and Flammable: keep away from fire and flame.

22
00:02:57.025 --> 00:03:02.729
Then hold them for 72 hours before use. The quarantine is part of the formulation.

23
00:03:03.729 --> 00:03:12.252
Every label needs name, net content, ingredients largest first, directions, cautions, maker, NAFDAC number and batch details.

24
00:03:12.697 --> 00:03:17.853
Ada in Lagos traced a thin bottle to its record in minutes, because of a code like this.

25
00:03:18.853 --> 00:03:24.776
At her desk, Comfort in Asaba added the three layers of cost and divided by 40 bottles.

26
00:03:25.236 --> 00:03:31.141
Packaging was almost as much as the liquid. So she shops for a cheaper pump before raising her price.

27
00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:38.014
Grow in steps, 20 kg, then 50 kg, then 100 kg, testing at each step.

28
00:03:39.014 --> 00:03:46.340
Hotels, schools and offices reorder every month. Ngozi ran a two-week trial, then quoted from real usage.

29
00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:57.220
On 30-day credit she must fund about ₦30,800 of stock each month. Put terms in writing, and never supply unregistered products to clinics.

30
00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:07.860
Now go through the lessons below. Make your dilution chart, your paper hand rub batch, your label set and your cost sheet, then prepare one institutional pitch.

31
00:04:08.286 --> 00:04:10.080
Well done for finishing the course.

